Correlix — licensing
====================

Correlix core is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. Commercial add-on modules are licensed under the Correlix Enterprise License (LicenseRef-Correlix-Enterprise) — see LICENSING.md.

Copyright 2026 Correlix

The two licence texts
---------------------

    Apache-2.0                      LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt
    LicenseRef-Correlix-Enterprise  LICENSES/Correlix-Enterprise.txt

Which files are under which licence
-----------------------------------

    LICENSING.md          the directory -> licence map. GENERATED from
                          licensing-policy.json; do not hand-edit.
    licensing-policy.json the machine-readable policy the map, the SPDX
                          headers and the CI boundary gate all read.

A file declares its own licence with an SPDX header:

    SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
    SPDX-License-Identifier: LicenseRef-Correlix-Enterprise

A directory under the Correlix Enterprise License also carries its own
LICENSE notice file naming that identifier.

DEFAULT: a file with no SPDX header, in a directory with no Enterprise
notice file, is Apache-2.0. The default is open, never commercial.

Third-party components
----------------------

Correlix redistributes third-party software under its own licences. Those
obligations are inventoried separately and are not affected by the split
above:

    NOTICE                        attribution and source offers
    docs/THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md  generated component inventory

Applying the Apache licence to your own contributions is described in the
appendix of LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt. Contributions to this repository
additionally require a signed Contributor License Agreement — see
CONTRIBUTING.md.
